      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T22:50:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Otherwise, it uploads a finger template from the fp_enc_buffer to the host.\n\u003e In Fpinfo version 2, we did not change the size of the template. \n\nWith the encryption we\u0027re using the encrypted size is the same as the original size IIRC. The case I\u0027m thinking about is where someone specifies a smaller-than-template capture type, does the capture, and then requests a template. Since the captured image is smaller than the template, is it going to copy the smaller image plus some garbage data?",
